Step 4 — Run the migration
```
dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef   # skip if already installed

cd IamEngine.Api
dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate --project ../IamEngine.Infrastructure
dotnet ef database update --project ../IamEngine.Infrastructure
```

Step - 5 (To confirm the migration actually applied and the DB file exists)

```
dotnet ef database update --project ../IamEngine.Infrastructure

ls -la // You should see iamengine.db in IamEngine.Api folder.

sqlite3 iamengine.db ".tables" // If you want to peek inside and confirm the Identity tables (AspNetUsers, AspNetRoles, etc.) plus your custom tables (ExternalIdentityMappings, ConnectorConfigs, ProvisioningEvents) actually got created
```
